FYDE-571: v3d minigbm: keep CMA for buffers a non-GPU engine actually walks

BCM2711/BCM2712 put no IOMMU in front of the display, codec and camera blocks:
the HVS scans out from a physical address and the VPU / rpivid / unicam V4L2
devices are all videobuf2-dma-contig, so buffers those engines walk have to be
physically contiguous. On a Pi that means CMA. v3d itself has an MMU, so a
buffer that is only rendered, textured or read by the CPU does not.

The backend was also routing every buffer carrying BO_USE_SW_MASK or
BO_USE_LINEAR into CMA. Those flags describe how the CPU touches a buffer, not
which engine has to walk it. CMA on a Pi is a small fixed reservation (cma-512)
that is at the same time the only source of scanout memory, so ordinary GPU and
CPU buffers filled and fragmented the pool until a 4K framebuffer -- 32 MiB in
one piece -- could no longer be allocated. An ARC kiosk app on a 4K display then
came up with every window state reporting "visible" and drew nothing, because
GraphicBufferAllocator was failing at 3840x2160.

Split the CMA condition in two and compose it:

  V3D_CONTIGUOUS_REQUIRED  codec / camera / sensor. No software fallback
                           exists for these, so a failure stays loud.
  V3D_CONTIGUOUS_SOFT      display and cursor. If CMA cannot satisfy them we
                           still hand back a usable buffer; it gets composited
                           by the GPU instead of promoted to a hardware plane.

V3D_LINEAR_USE is spelled out independently rather than derived from the
contiguous set, because narrowing what goes to CMA must never narrow what stays
linear: a buffer that leaves CMA must keep the layout its user already agreed
to, or a plain HW_COMPOSER surface would silently become UIF-tiled.

The #ifdef __ANDROID__ arm of V3D_CONTIGUOUS_SOFT is not used by this build and
is carried deliberately. The fydroid container ships its own build of this same
file, where the soft set is empty because Android never programs a KMS plane
there -- SurfaceFlinger runs with a Wayland composer and no hwcomposer HAL, so
the BO_USE_SCANOUT that cros_gralloc_helpers.cc derives from
GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER is meaningless inside the container. Keeping both arms
in one block keeps the two copies textually identical; they have silently
drifted before.

Scope: this is the host/Chrome half. Chrome does scan out, so BO_USE_SCANOUT
stays contiguous here and the allocation that failed in the bug still comes from
CMA on this side. The ARC half is the fydroid change above.

